<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Proj 2048 on Pencroff</title><link>https://pencroff.com/categories/proj-2048/</link><description>Recent content in Proj 2048 on Pencroff</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 05 Feb 2022 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://pencroff.com/categories/proj-2048/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Project 2048</title><link>https://pencroff.com/project/proj-2048/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pencroff.com/project/proj-2048/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Play yourself or see how AI can move tiles across board.&#10;Try to defeat AI :)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="demo"&gt;Demo&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;iframe src="//pencroff.github.io/proj2048/" title="Project 2048"&#10; width="500" height="800"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"&#10; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Please check:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="//github.com/Pencroff/proj2048"&gt;Github repo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="//pencroff.github.io/proj2048/"&gt;Demo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>Proj 2048</title><link>https://pencroff.com/post/proj-2048/</link><pubDate>Sat, 05 Feb 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pencroff.com/post/proj-2048/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A few years ago Gabriele Cirulli developed a sliding puzzle where the goal is to grow tiles and get up to 2048. My&#10;“Proj 2048” is about implementing several agents to play. Which should get tiles up to 4096 or maybe even 64536 (if&#10;it’s possible of course) 😉.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>